{# ============================================================
	HC SVG FILTERS  —  src/_includes/hc-svg-filters.njk
	============================================================

	Inline SVG filter definitions used by high-contrast.css.

	Currently defines:
	  - #hc-duotone-custom — duotone for .high-contrast-custom
	    (#010080 navy → #fff white).

	Included once from base.njk near </body>. The <svg> element
	itself is sized to 0×0 and absolutely positioned so it never
	renders; only its <filter> defs are referenced from CSS via
	`filter: url(#hc-duotone-custom)`.

	WHY HERE INSTEAD OF IN CSS?
	---------------------------
	SVG filters can be embedded as data: URIs in CSS, but that
	makes them harder to read and edit, and Firefox in particular
	has been flaky about referencing filters from data: URIs in
	the past. Inlining the SVG once per page is the cleanest path.

	IF YOU CHANGE THE CUSTOM PALETTE
	--------------------------------
	The tableValues below encode the endpoints of the duotone:
	shadow color (#010080) on the LEFT, highlight color (#fff)
	on the RIGHT.

	  #010080 normalized = (1/255, 0/255, 128/255)
	                    = (0.0039, 0,    0.5020)

	If you change --hc-fg / --hc-bg in high-contrast.css for
	.high-contrast-custom, recompute these tableValues to match.
	============================================================ #}
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
     width="0"
     height="0"
     style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden"
     aria-hidden="true"
     focusable="false">
	<filter id="hc-duotone-custom">
		<feColorMatrix type="matrix" values="
			0.33 0.33 0.33 0 0
			0.33 0.33 0.33 0 0
			0.33 0.33 0.33 0 0
			0    0    0    1 0"/>
		<feComponentTransfer color-interpolation-filters="sRGB">
			{# shadows → bg (#010080), highlights → fg (#fff) #}
			<feFuncR type="table" tableValues="0.0039 1"/>
			<feFuncG type="table" tableValues="0      1"/>
			<feFuncB type="table" tableValues="0.5020 1"/>
		</feComponentTransfer>
	</filter>
</svg>
